# Review package: batch 9, slice harness

## f76abd60 Run the real tests against the company's Postgres 17.11 too

PGlite is Postgres 18 in WASM with one connection, so what the fences and the locks need, a real server and transactions
that wait on each other, cannot show there. run.sh now starts the image compose's db runs, with a password made at run
time and the port on 127.0.0.1, and hands HH_REAL_PG to vitest. pg.ts gives each test file a database of its own and drops
it with the agents' roles, which belong to the server and would outlive it.

compose.test.ts holds run.sh to compose's db: the image now, and each -c as soon as compose has a command.

Two debts of plan 1b fall to this harness, in auth-locks.test.ts: moveOlderSession's lock on the person's row and the
sign-in limit's one transaction were tested only by shape. Neither test rests on timing: a client of its own holds the lock
open and the test goes on when pg_stat_activity says the others wait. All three pass, and each was seen red on a run with
the lock taken away and the old row marked as moved: [200, 401], 1 session left, and 35 tries let through instead of 30
(runs/remote-p3t1-bite-*.log, never committed).

Ruling: compose's db has no command until Plan 2 Task 7, so the case reads the image and the command from compose and checks each -c when it is there - why: the lead's note; the case then bites by itself - cost if wrong: a setting of Task 7's that run.sh lacks turns this case red, which is what it is for.
Ruling: with HH_REAL_PG set run.sh starts no Postgres but still starts Pebble - why: acme.test.ts needs Pebble whichever Postgres is used - cost if wrong: a Docker run a Postgres-only caller did not need.
Ruling: a test beyond the one per debt the lead named, a disable during a hand-over - why: two hand-overs share the person's lock, so they pass with it gone; the disable is the race that lock is for - cost if wrong: one more real test of about a second.
Ruling: pg.ts also exports poolOf, beyond the plan's two - why: openDb answers only the database and a test has to end its connections, in two files so far - cost if wrong: one line.

